# NEMO 44.1 — YOUTUBE: JS RUNTIME + EJS SOLVER + PO-TOKEN SCRIPT MODE (hotfix)
#   /ytdoctor showed the truth: "n challenge solving failed ... Ensure you have a
#   supported JavaScript runtime and challenge solver script" — modern yt-dlp
#   needs a JS runtime (node/deno) AND the yt-dlp-ejs solver package to unlock
#   YouTube formats; nobody had told it to use the Node 18 already on the box.
#   Separately, the bgutil PO-token plugin was probing an HTTP server that does
#   not exist (its default), because script mode never got built (needs Node 20+).
#   Fixes:
#     · engine now passes --js-runtime node (deno if present) and
#       --remote-components ejs:github so yt-dlp can fetch its solver scripts
#     · /ytfix — one command: installs yt-dlp[default] + yt-dlp-ejs, verifies the
#       solver, and re-probes; shows before/after
#     · /ytpot install — checks Node major version; on <20 gives the exact
#       NodeSource two-liner instead of failing silently; on success verifies the
#       script actually generates a token
#     · error classifier knows JSRUNTIME; /ytdoctor reports JS runtime + EJS status
